(ns kotoba.compiler.guest-grammar-vendor-test
  "This repository carries a BYTE COPY of kotoba-lang's `lang/guest-grammar.edn`
  at `resources/kotoba/lang/guest-grammar.edn`, and it owns the frontend the
  file is supposed to describe. Two things can go wrong, and both had.

  ## Why the existing check could not see either

  kotoba-lang's `local-and-sibling-vendors-match-authority` compares its
  authority against `../amu`, `../kotoba`, `../kotoba-sema` and `../grammar`.
  Those paths exist only inside the west monorepo layout, each is guarded with
  `(when (.isFile ...))`, and an absent path is reported `:missing` and
  tolerated. In a single-repository clone it compares exactly one copy -- the
  authority's own -- and reports green.

  Measured 2026-09-03 on the four mains, before the resync wave: amu's copy was
  one change behind (580 lines against 601) and kotoba's two copies were two
  hundred lines behind. Three of four had drifted, and the check written to
  find drift said nothing. ADR-2608136000's shape: a check that could not run
  returns the value of a check that ran and found nothing wrong.

  ## What this file checks instead

  1. The copy this repository ships is byte-identical to the authority of the
     2026-09-03 wave, by pinned sha256. That literal is pinned in FOUR
     repositories (kotoba-lang, amu, kotoba, here), so an authority edit that
     is not carried to all four goes red in the ones left behind -- including
     in a clone with no sibling to compare against.
  2. The copy AGREES WITH THE FRONTEND. `:admitted-builtins` must name exactly
     the heads `kernel-memory-operations`, `slice-value-operations` and
     `kernel-privileged-operations` admit. This is the check no other
     repository can make, because the frontend lives here.

  Measured 2026-09-03: the authority named THREE kernel heads
  (`kernel-load-u8`, `kernel-store-u8`, `kernel-boot-info`) while this
  frontend admitted 114 -- 115 since fwstore's `kernel-uefi-alloc-region`.
  Nothing here, in amu or in kotoba-lang reads
  `:admitted-builtins`, and nothing anywhere reads it to decide what the
  COMPILER admits -- the tables below do that. Its one reader is
  `kotoba.grammar/admitted-heads` in kotoba-lang/kotoba's vendored loader,
  where a missing head is reported as `:unknown-form`. So the understatement
  cost one repository 112 false `:unknown-form` reports and nothing failed,
  through eight widenings of the tables it describes.

  ## The one thing this file cannot do

  Only one copy of `kotoba/lang/guest-grammar.edn` is on this repository's
  classpath: its own. None of `artifact`, `kotoba-hir` or `kotoba-kir` carries
  one. So the `COMPARED` count here is 1 and the cross-repository half is done
  by the pinned digest, not by a comparison. amu and kotoba each see two and
  three copies respectively and compare them across their pins."
  (:require [kotoba.lang.edn :as edn]
            [kotoba.io :as io]
            [kotoba.lang.coll :as set]
            [kotoba.lang.text :as str]
            [kotoba.test :refer [deftest is testing]]
            [kotoba.compiler.frontend :as frontend]
            [kotoba.sema :as sema]
            [kotoba.compiler.guest-grammar-contract-test :as contract]))

(def authority-grammar-sha256
  "sha256 of kotoba-lang `lang/guest-grammar.edn`.

  Advanced 2026-09-05 again for the string-search surface slice
  (string-index-of / string-contains? / string-split-count in :predicates).
  Advanced 2026-09-05 to `9d701ea9` with the kbb slice 2 string heads
  (env-read + fs-browse; prior authority #550 was `811e3d5e`). The authority
  grammar moved and this repository's vendored copy moves with it in the same
  commit, keeping the lockstep contract.

  kotoba-lang moves with this commit. amu and kotoba are BEHIND until each
  resyncs, and each one's own pin still matches its own copy, so neither goes
  red on its own main -- but amu's
  `every-classpath-copy-of-the-grammar-is-the-same-grammar` compares ITS copy
  against the one in the kotoba-sema it pins, so amu's pin advance and its
  grammar resync have to be the same commit (amu ADR 0330's postscript).

  Advanced 2026-09-07 to `e333abac` for amu-h7: `:admitted-builtins` gains
  `kernel-undefined-opcode-handler-address`, the fifty-fifth privileged head
  (kotoba-lang#PR carries the authority; amu and kotoba resync after).

  Advanced 2026-09-11 to `10ff0062` for module type parameters (root ADR
  adr-2609113100; authority kotoba-lang 9c2bb949): `:core-form-shapes` gains
  `:ns` and `:require-spec` -- the `(:params [sym ...])` module clause and the
  `:require [ns :as a :with {sym type}]` binding -- and `:admission-limits`
  gains `:max-template-parameters 8`. No head admitted or withdrawn; the
  previous digest was `515bbc7d`.

  Advanced 2026-09-11 to `5a5a3d6c` for the ns attr-map spelling (authority
  kotoba-lang 1c7934ba): `:core-form-shapes :ns` gains `ATTR-MAP?` and an
  `:attr-map` entry -- `{:kotoba/export [...]}` after the docstring means
  `(:export [...])`, and the frontend in THIS commit implements it
  (`namespace-attr-map->clauses`, one validation path). No head admitted or
  withdrawn; the previous digest was `10ff0062`.

  Advanced 2026-09-11 to `7262fae3` for `:refer` in a require spec (authority
  kotoba-lang f69b6a3d): `:core-form-shapes :require-spec` admits
  `[m :refer [f]]` / `[m :as a :refer [f]]` -- implemented by amu's project
  linker, which is the only place a `:require` clause is ever read -- and
  gains `:ns-refused-clauses`, which THIS commit implements in the frontend
  (`namespace-refused-clauses`: `:import` and its kin are refused by name).
  No head admitted or withdrawn; the previous digest was `5a5a3d6c`.

  Advanced 2026-09-11 to `d07b8816` for `:refer-clojure` as a no-op
  (authority kotoba-lang): `:core-form-shapes :ns :clauses` gains
  `:refer-clojure` and `:ns` a `:refer-clojure` entry -- `(:refer-clojure
  :exclude [..])` / `(:refer-clojure :only [..])` is admitted as a NO-OP,
  which THIS commit implements in the frontend
  (`validate-refer-clojure-clauses!`: shape-checked, `:rename` refused by
  name, then dropped before the clause loop), and `:refer-clojure` leaves
  `:ns-refused-clauses`. No head admitted or withdrawn; the previous digest
  was `7262fae3`.

  Advanced 2026-09-11 to `48fb5241` for the heterogeneous keyword-map
  literal (authority kotoba-lang): `:sugar :map-literal :value-types
  :keyword-keys` becomes a map -- a keyword-keyed literal with a value that
  spells a non-i64 type lowers to a closed record read off its values, which
  THIS commit implements in the frontend (`keyword-map-literal-record-fields`
  / `map-literal-record-type` in `desugar-map`; the all-i64 keyword literal
  is unchanged byte for byte), and `:entry-limits` gains `:keyword-record 20`.
  No head admitted or withdrawn; the previous digest was `d07b8816`.

  Advanced 2026-09-11 to `8450745f` for the computed module constant
  (authority kotoba-lang): `:core-form-shapes` gains `:def` -- a `def` whose
  value is a pure call form folds at analysis time, which THIS commit
  implements in the frontend (`fold-def-value!`: a one-function probe module
  over the constants above it, analysed by `analyze-forms*`, an empty effect
  row required, executed once on the reference interpreter at
  `def-fold-fuel`, the result spelled back by `spell-folded-value`; the
  stateful heads and the rest refused by name). No head admitted or
  withdrawn; the previous digest was `48fb5241`.

  Advanced 2026-09-11 to `c308cc04`, the same wave's second step: a quoted
  SYMBOL at a def is named as quoted data (it was answered as an alias
  lookup) and a string past the portable byte bound is refused by the bound
  (both in `def-parts`, THIS commit). No head admitted or withdrawn; the
  previous digest was `8450745f`.

  Advanced 2026-09-11 to `11fd920c` for the map callback (authority
  kotoba-lang): `:sugar :map` gains `:callback` -- the admitted shapes by
  name and eight refusals, one per cause, in place of the one sentence
  `N-source map fn requires matching unique parameters and one expression`
  (THIS commit splits it in the `map` desugar, refuses a literal / partial /
  comp callback by name, and makes the stored-callback path REQUEST its
  dispatcher). No head admitted or withdrawn; the previous digest was
  `c308cc04`.

  Advanced 2026-09-12 to `63dc6e9a` for `map-indexed` (authority kotoba-lang,
  adr-2609111900): `:sugar` gains `:map-indexed` -- a new head admitted
  between `:map` and `:filter`, IMPLEMENTATION STATE not a property (the
  wall measured at amu 10469db0 against 225 sources was stdlib coverage --
  `unknown operation: map-indexed is not a builtin, a sugar head, or a
  function of this module` -- not a designed exclusion). The callback reuses
  `:map :callback`'s admission verbatim (THIS commit implements it in the
  frontend, a new `map-indexed` case clause: named / inline / closure-value
  callback of fixed arity two, index first, requesting its dispatcher
  exactly as `map`'s stored callback does; a one-parameter callback is
  refused by name -- `map-indexed passes the index first` -- ahead of the
  generic count sentence; a module's own `map-indexed` is kept, the
  into/mapv rule). One head ADMITTED; the previous digest was `11fd920c`.

  NOT advanced for `7644f32d` (2026-09-12, the merge of the variadic defn
  wave 53e4d2f0 and the map-indexed wave 63dc6e9a): main e4e9521 carried the
  COPY at 7644f32d and left this literal at 63dc6e9a -- this file is `.clj`
  under a `.cljk` name and no runner here executes it since the rename, so
  nothing said so. Recorded rather than silently skipped, as kotoba-lang's
  own history vector records its skip of b957f5cd.

  Advanced 2026-09-12 to `5b8af0f9` for the implicit-do body of `defn` /
  `defn-` / `fn` (authority kotoba-lang, adr-2609111900): `:implicit-body-
  forms` moves the three heads from `:refuses` to `:sequences` -- several
  body forms collapse to `do`, as `let`'s do, IMPLEMENTATION STATE not a
  property (`do` is a first-class head on every backend, so the widening is
  a spelling). THIS commit implements it in the frontend (`implicit-do-body`,
  applied in `defn-parts`, `lift-lambda`, and the map / map-indexed / reduce /
  filter inline-callback sites; empty bodies, `loop`, `try` and protocol
  methods keep their refusals). No head admitted or withdrawn; the previous
  digest was `7644f32d`.

  Advanced 2026-09-12 to `e16c74e5` for quoted symbol data (authority
  kotoba-lang 82e27337, adr-2609111900): `:def :value :quoted` admits
  `'sym` / `'#{a b}` / `'{a 1 b 2}` / `'[a b]` as literals, held as written
  and lowered to the forms `(symbol \"...\")` and the typed constructors
  already lower to -- IMPLEMENTATION STATE not a property (`:symbol` was a
  value type; only the literal spelling was missing; measurement 18: 12 of
  225 compiler sources, the operation tables). THIS commit implements it in
  the frontend (`quote-form?`, `quoted-symbol-datum-kind`,
  `desugar-quoted-datum`, `constant-literal?`, `spell-folded-value`,
  `def-parts`); mixed collections, non-scalar map values and a quoted list
  refused by name. No head admitted or withdrawn (`quote` is elaborated
  away and reaches no backend); the previous digest was `5b8af0f9`.

  Advanced 2026-09-12 to `295457fd` for typed closure parameters (authority
  kotoba-lang 22180120, merged a6807a73, adr-2609111900): `:callable-type
  :parameter-types` moves from `#{:i64}` to `:closure-result-types` -- a
  closure PARAMETER type is admitted exactly when it is admitted as a
  closure RESULT type, one predicate (`closure-result-type?`) on both
  sides. IMPLEMENTATION STATE not a property: the dispatcher and the
  lambda's helper were already ordinary typed KIR functions; only the
  parameter side had never been written (measurements 16-19: the
  clojure.walk twin's walk / prewalk / postwalk, 19 modules). THIS commit
  implements it in the frontend (`validate-value-type!`, `dispatcher-key` /
  `dispatcher-parameter-label` / `invoke-dispatcher-name`,
  `desugar-lexical-call`, `lift-lambda`, `lambda-dispatchers`,
  `desugar-ordinary-call`, `*function-callable-param-contracts*`); a
  callable or linear parameter and a type outside the result profile are
  refused by name; an all-i64 contract program keeps its HIR / KIR digests
  (typed_closure_parameters_test). No head admitted or withdrawn; the
  previous digest was `e16c74e5`.

  Advanced 2026-09-16 to `9ecd9dbc` (kotoba-lang #693): `:predicates` gains
  `arena-scope` (root ADR-2609160044, context ABI v6) and the four ABI v7
  text heads `string-compare` / `string-fold-ascii` / `string-find-blank` /
  `string-skip-blank`, each declared with its contract. Five heads
  admitted, none withdrawn; this frontend's tables carry the same five.

  Advanced 2026-09-16 again to `72648a8c` (kotoba-lang #694): `:predicates`
  gains the two ABI v8 line heads `string-index-of-from` /
  `string-compare-lines`. Two heads admitted, none withdrawn; this
  frontend's tables carry the same two.

  Advanced 2026-09-16 again to `8a2913b8` (kotoba-lang #696): the two ABI v10
  range heads `string-find-byte` / `string-append-range`. Two heads
  admitted, none withdrawn; this frontend's tables carry the same two.

  Advanced 2026-09-23 to `0f98fd74` (kotoba-lang #704,
  ADR-reliability-t54b-max-parameters-64): `:admission-limits`
  `:max-parameters` 5 -> 64. No head admitted or withdrawn; this
  frontend's `max-parameters` moved to 64 in bf42c45.

  Advanced 2026-09-24 to `bdbc8474` (adr-2609242100 P1, lang/limits.edn):
  `:admission-limits :max-set-items` 16 -> 32 (this frontend's
  `max-typed-set-items` was already 32), the `:string-bound` sentence 4096
  -> 65536, the variadic `:abi-bound` 5 -> 64. No head admitted or
  withdrawn; this frontend's `max-type-depth` / `max-schema-depth` moved
  8 -> 12 in the same commit.

  Advanced 2026-09-25 to `d87fe28a` (lang/state-ability.edn, slice 1):
  `:sugar :state-ability` admits `defhandler` / `with` / `resume`; this
  frontend's expand-state-ability-forms / specialize-state-abilities /
  thread-state-abilities land in the same commit.

  Advanced 2026-09-25 to `d71c8b00` (superproject adr-2609242330):
  `:predicates` admits the eight bytes heads and `:bytes-value` records the
  decision; this frontend types the three new heads (`bytes-from-vector-i64`,
  `vector-i64-from-bytes`, `string-from-utf8`) in the same commit.
  Advanced 2026-09-25 to `5e71ffed` (superproject adr-2609242330, the
  selfhost builtin gaps): `:library-heads` and the `:string-equality` /
  `:true?` / `:integer?` sugar, implemented by this frontend's
  `expand-intrinsic-helper-forms` and type-directed rewrite in the same
  commit; the `:throw` note admits a loop body.
  Advanced 2026-09-26 to `e2a90a2a` (superproject adr-2609242330, gap 3 of
  the selfhost foundation): `:sugar` `:type-predicates` -- the predicates ask
  a :document its kind -- implemented by this frontend's type-directed
  rewrite in the same commit.
  Advanced 2026-09-26 to `407357fd` (superproject adr-2609242330, gap 1 of
  the selfhost foundation): `:sugar :expression-absence` -- a missing else
  and a literal nil are absence, typed by the present branch -- implemented
  by this frontend's absence markers in the same commit.
  Advanced 2026-09-26 to `b70bb39e` (kotoba-gmir ADR 0031, aiueos ADR-0222):
  the admitted kernel head `kernel-dequant-dot-ptq1-0`, with this frontend's
  arity and base-position rows in the same commit.
  Advanced 2026-10-09 to `4f7f138f` (root ADR-2610092330 / ADR-2610092310
  S2): `:operations-registry` points at kotoba-lang's lang/operations.edn,
  and the `:bytes-value` note records the :bytes / :link document kinds this
  frontend now types (document-fixed-operations, same commit). No head
  admitted or withdrawn.
  Advanced 2026-10-09 to `da68c3fa`: the `:portable-string-symbol-values`
  note, the `:data-host-arg` note and the string-index comment say the
  portable string bound is 65536 UTF-8 bytes, not 127 (amu
  kotoba.compiler.limits, unified 2026-09-24). Notes only; no head admitted
  or withdrawn."
  contract/authority-grammar-sha256)

(def ^:private resource-path "kotoba/lang/guest-grammar.edn")

(defn- sha256-hex [^bytes bs]
  (let [d (.digest (java.security.MessageDigest/getInstance "SHA-256") bs)]
    (apply str (map #(format "%02x" %) d))))

(defn- classpath-copies
  "Every copy of the grammar resource on this classpath, as [url bytes]. Not
  `io/resource`, which answers with the FIRST and so cannot see a second."
  []
  (->> (enumeration-seq (.getResources (clojure.lang.RT/baseLoader) resource-path))
       (mapv (fn [url]
               [(str url)
                (with-open [in (.openStream url)]
                  (.readAllBytes in))]))))

(defn- head-names [x]
  (into #{} (map name) x))

(defn- frontend-kernel-heads []
  ;; Through the same public accessor a CONSUMER has to use
  ;; (`kotoba.sema/kernel-operation-heads`), not the three tables directly.
  ;; The tables are still asserted below, because this repository owns them
  ;; and an accessor that silently lost a family would otherwise pass.
  (head-names sema/kernel-operation-heads))

(defn- grammar-kernel-heads [grammar]
  (into #{} (filter #(or (str/starts-with? % "kernel-")
                         (str/starts-with? % "slice-")))
        (head-names (:admitted-builtins grammar))))

(deftest the-vendored-copy-is-the-authority-of-the-resync-wave
  (let [copies (classpath-copies)]
    (println (format "COMPARED\t%d\tclasspath copies of %s" (count copies) resource-path))
    (is (pos? (count copies))
        "the grammar resource is not on the classpath at all; this run measured
         nothing, which is not the same as finding nothing wrong")
    (doseq [[url bytes] copies]
      (let [actual (sha256-hex bytes)]
        (is (= authority-grammar-sha256 actual)
            (str "vendored grammar drifted from the authority\n"
                 "  copy     " url "\n"
                 "  expected " authority-grammar-sha256 "\n"
                 "  actual   " actual "\n"
                 "Resync from kotoba-lang lang/guest-grammar.edn and carry the"
                 " digest to kotoba-lang, amu, kotoba-sema and kotoba together."))))))

(deftest the-grammar-names-exactly-the-kernel-heads-this-frontend-admits
  (let [grammar (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource resource-path)))
        declared (grammar-kernel-heads grammar)
        admitted (frontend-kernel-heads)
        missing (set/difference admitted declared)
        extra (set/difference declared admitted)]
    (println (format "SCANNED\t%d\tkernel heads admitted by the frontend (%d declared by the grammar)"
                     (count admitted) (count declared)))
    (is (pos? (count admitted))
        "the frontend admits no kernel head at all; the tables were not read")
    (is (empty? missing)
        (str "the frontend admits heads the authority does not name: "
             (pr-str (sort missing))))
    (is (empty? extra)
        (str "the authority names heads the frontend does not admit: "
             (pr-str (sort extra))))
    (testing "the accessor is the union of the three tables, so a family
              dropped from it -- or a table emptied by a bad merge -- is not a
              pass"
      (is (= admitted
             (head-names (concat (keys frontend/kernel-memory-operations)
                                 (keys frontend/slice-value-operations)
                                 (keys frontend/kernel-privileged-operations))))))
    (testing "and the tables are non-empty"
      (is (= 53 (count frontend/kernel-memory-operations)))
      (is (= 8 (count frontend/slice-value-operations)))
      ;; fwstore: 54 since `kernel-uefi-alloc-region`; amu-h7: 55 since
      ;; `kernel-undefined-opcode-handler-address`.
      (is (= 55 (count frontend/kernel-privileged-operations))))))
